Parliament did not support an amendment to free Tymoshenko
Ukraine's parliament has today rejected the proposal to repeal the amendment of the section of the Criminal Code condemning opposition leader Yulia Tymoshenko.
The modification would open the doors to the release of the former prime minister, but parliamentarians rejected the proposal to reduce penalties for economic crimes at second reading.
In October, Tymoshenko was sentenced to seven years in prison for the alleged signing of a disadvantaged agreement for Ukraine on the purchase of natural gas.
The sentence is not yet firm, the appellate court has an obligation to review it in December.
Tymoshenko was convinced that it was a political revenge of the regime, and even in the West there have been doubts about the impartiality of the tribunal.
The proposal to withdraw paragraph 365 of the Criminal Code condemning the former prime minister was supported by 147 deputies in the vote.
226 votes were required for approval.
The Victory of Libya
The history of Libyan liberation, or of the Libyan rebellion, already has its losers.
Muammar el-Gaddafi was buried in a secret place in the desert and without him there is no war anymore.
It remains to define who the winner is
As usual in the region, the Islamists won the elections, but now it is about elucidating whether they are moderates or radicals
The National Transitional Council has brought into force the traditional law, the Sharia, which we already know.
Libya will become a country without crime, because thieves will have their hand cut off.
Women can already forget to emancipate and apostates waiting for their execution and so on.
Instead of the person of the dictator, society, composed of warrior tribes, will be united by the Quran.
In Libya there will be an order that we cannot even imagine and that we certainly cannot.
However, our way of life is neither the only nor objectively the best and probably did not suit the aforementioned Libyans.
The truth is that it does not cease to be surprising that Islamic fighters gratefully accepted the help of unfaithful dogs.
The only justification was that, from their point of view, the NATO attacks were not led by an American general, but great is Allah, whose greatness they celebrated after each of the successful interventions.
When they are looking for victors in Libya, the West is not among them.
We are caught up in a shooting that Islamists and our politicians serve to get rid of a dictator in the person of a political ally with no guarantees of profit.
Following the recent bad experiences in Afghanistan and Iraq, we do not occupy Libya militarily.
In this case, it’s not a problem for locals to expel the “crusaders”
But, without occupation, will the oil companies manage to seize Libyan black gold only with good words?
It’s quite possible not, but it may be that the West can finally boast of protecting human rights.
As long as the followers of the Sharia do not cross us.
A new era of the crisis begins
France and the rest of Europe are on the hunt for an investor seeker
A statistical whirlwind has spread across Europe
Individual states have released their GDP data for Q3.
The Czech economy in the quarter-on-quarter period has stagnated, while France and Germany have grown.
However, the bond market today has broken records.
Investors are no longer fixed only in Italy, but also in Spain, France, Austria and others.
Statistical cabinets in Eurozone, Germany, the Czech Republic and other European countries have already released their preliminary estimates on economic growth in the third quarter.
Germany’s GDP grew by 0.5%, France’s 0.4%
Both countries have made public the data of the second quarter, in Germany it has improved more than expected (growth of 0.3% instead of expected 0.1%), although in France there was a slight reduction of 0.1% (the original data spoke of stagnation).
The Czech economy grew 1.5% year-on-year in the third quarter of this year.
However, in the quarter-month period, gross domestic product (GDP) has stagnated and according to the ČS�Ú the trend towards a gradual slowdown in the growth of economic development is shaped.
The results are even worse than analyst forecasts.
Main events:
Year-on-year, the Czech economy grew in the third quarter of this year by 1.5%, but quarterly has stagnated.
In the third quarter, the German economy, according to pre-data and recalculated seasonally, grew by 0.5%.
The economy of the Eurozone and also of the European Union, between July and September and compared to the previous quarter, grew by 0.2%, which coincides with the expectations of analysts.
The Greek economy has fallen 5.2% year-on-year.
Ten-year bond interest is 28.45%.
Interest in Italian and Spanish bonds has grown to critical limits.
The problematic situation also begins to affect Austria, Holland, France, Belgium, etc.
Ten-year Czech bond interest remains at 4%, albeit in the area the situation is getting worse.
In Germany, voices are raised that say that the ECB should ultimately grant loans.
Czecks qualify for the European Championship.
They won 1:0 and celebrate qualifying with a 200 million premium.
The football team fulfills the most difficult task of the entire season!
In Montenegro, thanks to the excellent Čech and the brilliant goalkeeper Petr Jiráček, there was a 1:0 victory.
The Czech team, along with a good dose of luck in the second half, defended fantastically from the attacks of the local team, so it will not miss the appointment of the European championship.
IHNED.cz followed the development of the party in detail in a thorough report.
There was almost no excitement in the first half and a good dose of luck in the second.
The Czech team, thanks to the collapse of the local team towards the end, and also the excellent game of Čech and the heroic Jiráček, won by 1:0 in Montenegro and celebrates its pass to the European Championship.
Because of the very correct Czech defense, the Montenegrins did not press until the second half.
The two victims of the match were Damjanovič and Vučinič, who missed two great occasions.
In addition, thanks to the great Petr Čech, the Czech eleven will not miss the appointment of the European Cup, so the coffers of national football will receive an approximate gratification of 200 million crowns.
Already from the first minutes there was a good offensive game.
Both teams insisted only on maintaining the lines and played nothing more around midfield.
There was no pressure from the local players in the first half, kicks to the other field in defense, precisely what the Czech defense knew how to avoid.
Iranian students are willing to die from their country’s nuclear program.
They formed a human shield.
Several hundred university students formed human shields around nuclear facilities in Iran.
With their gesture they want to express their support for their country’s nuclear program in the face of a possible Israeli attack.
The students prayed at noon Tuesday outside the facility and then chanted death slogans to the U.S. and Israel.
Several hundreds of university students formed human shields around the nuclear technological center working with uranium on Tuesday.
They intend to demonstrate that they are willing to defend their country’s nuclear program with their own lives.
The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA), in a recent report, found that Iran, according to all indications, strives for nuclear weapons.
There is talk in Israel of a possible attack on Iranian nuclear facilities.
The students prayed at noon at Isfahan’s nuclear facilities and then launched death slogans against the U.S. and Israel.
In the event of an attack, whose objective would be to paralyze the Iranian nuclear program would be reached, according to Israeli sources, not only the Isfahan power plant, but also Natanz facilities, where uranium is enriched.
Diary menu of an obese child: don't eat breakfast and dinner
More than a third of children aged between 9 and 13 have overweight problems, where overweight affects 9% of the school population and obesity at 5%.
Obese children come mostly from families with an unhealthy lifestyle, according to current research.
It again demonstrates what is the importance of the environment where it grows for a healthy development of the person, as well as the models that serve as a reference.
At the table, obsessed children feed, for example, on sausages at least twice as often as children from families with normal weight.
For dinner, more than 19% of the obese had dinned chips the day before the analysis, which is linked to the “Obesibity prevention program is not a coincidence”.
In families of overweight children there is no habit of playing sports, which applies to most current families, where only 15% of children responded that their parents, at least once a week, find time for physical exercise.
Survey of 900 Children
The survey was carried out at the end of last school year and almost 900 children of Basic Education from all over the Czech Republic participated.
It was already the second edition of the "Obesity is not a coincidence" program, supported by the General Health Insurance Company and Unilever.
So far, more than 12 thousand children have participated in the project from the 4th to the 8th course.
An adequate diet and enough exercise in the family are determining factors, which significantly decrease the number of children who are overweight and even obese.
“Only half of the children surveyed have responded that they have five meals a day depending on the regimen: breakfast, lunch, lunch and dinner, which is one of the basic conditions for a healthy diet.”
No breakfast but sausaged for dinner
Specialists warn that, in a healthy development, details are also important, which also count, such as having a fixed hour for family breakfast.
In the Czech Republic, however, only 23 per cent of schoolers have breakfast at the same time.
In most families, everyone eats breakfast alone.
But the worst thing was to find out that in 10% of households nothing eats.
Breakfast, however, is the basis of a correct daily diet.
The study shows that families of obese children are consumed much more often the insane potato chips.
Almost all - regardless of weight - drink daily sweet soft drinks (70%).
As a general rule, more than 40% of the children surveyed do sports, however, among their parents this result is reduced to less than half, only 15%.
Embrace your diet
The next phase of the study made it possible for the chosen children (204 boys and 172 girls from 13 schools) to create their own diets from all possible offers according to their tastes and opinions.
"Czech children's food preferences between the ages of 12 and 15, from the point of view of healthy eating, are far removed from the ideal."
Among his favorite foods are pasta, meat and candy
"It's above alarming the popularity of candy sodas," the study's final report said.
As the main food, the pasta is taken and the poultry is closely followed.
Practically, children always reject legume and the taste for fish and vegetables is very low.
Shift to Healthy Habits
At the same time, the study shows that children are willing to change their eating habits if they receive fair information.
"In the control group of the participants in the study, who completed the questionnaire after finishing the prevention program "Obesity is not a coincidence", there was in many cases an important change in favor of the principles of a healthy diet," the results of the study said.
It draws attention, for example, to sweet sodas, where many children would begin to prefer ordinary water.
Children would also more frequently choose poultry meat and fish for the main meal in the questionnaire and restrict the consumption of sweet food and flour derivatives.
The stylist must also be a good psychologist, the professionals argue
In the introductory article, How Stylists Learn, I already complained a bit that the initial lessons were already quite loaded.
I had no idea how that would go.
Lectures of three professionals of the field, how to dress in problematic characters and, in addition, a seminar on how it works in the world of entertainment.
And it's gonna be worse.
The closer the final exams are, the more information and handicapped tasks await us
And although the course takes place every Saturday and Sunday, there is no longer a pin.
We are time we have studied with the director, Alena, (in the course there is no man) on how to dress the woman who does not have a perfect symmetry.
And that's the vast majority.
Someone is nude, someone has a stylized figure without the right curves and someone is overweight.
The stylist must know how to optically soften wide shoulders, lengthen a neck or recreate the necessary curves
They have given us certain tricks on how to highlight the body of women of Jennifer Lopez's type, of huge breasts and hips but narrow waist and at the same time not to dress it in an overly defiant way
If, for example, the difference between the waist and the hips is so much that the skirt or pants do not adapt, it is worthwhile to sew at least one piece of extra fabric to measure.
They certainly won't regret it, because the clothes they feel perfectly are unpayable.
With a tailored skirt you’ll feel much better than with one that doesn’t stop moving, getting up, dancing at the waist, etc.
The stylized body can be allowed to wear clothes with folds, ornaments, embroidery or draping.
There are certainly many types of diverse and body information, so I’m happy that I have the whole week to put order on my head all this information.
And even so, I'm afraid that with the assigned task, I've got more than enough.
Each participant in the course has been assigned two celebrities, who must design two costumes: one for the day and one for the night.
You have to take into account the current aspect, the style of fashion that suits the person in question.
I've had Miranda Kerr "dress up", you may know her from the Victoria's Secret campaign.
Screaming inside, for me it is much better that, for example, Britney Spears or Christina Aguilera, who lately will have gained about a hundred kilos (please take into account the exaggeration), or the young Selena Gomez.
The dresses have to cut them from the magazines or look for them on the Internet and print them, and then elaborate them graphically.
The moodboard, which is called the complete result, also expresses our personal style and our relationship with graphic design.
It’s also important to think about the graphic part of styling.
The stylist, therefore, not only physically dresses, but also deals, for example, with the pages of products in magazines (of specific topics, such as trends, bags, coats, etc.).
The stylist and designer Mario Kameník told us all about this.
But all of this remains for Sunday.
The stylist must have a global vision.
The three specialist guests cheered Saturday’s conference with information about all kinds of bodies.
Stylist Honza Pokorný, fashion designer Jakub Polanka and fashion photographer Ben Renč.
Jakub reminded us that fashion is an illusion and the stylist should know how to take advantage of this.
And a good stylist knows how to work with the same garment in various ways.
Variability in this case is essential.
Thus, such trench-coat (or as they say in English) you can dress the classic with jeans and T-shirt, but it also serves to dress the naked body with heeled shoes and photograph it as if it were actually a dress.
Or it is enough to roll it up and raise its neck to get a totally different image.
"Play with it," he insisted.
What I value most is the following advice: "To start working, you must first know all the rules."
"Then you can break them," Jakub said.
At last it is clear to me why we memorize all those formulas, what is combined with what, why, if then it turns out that in fashion magazines we find different results.
That's without talking about parades.
Thanks to photographer Ben, I know that a stylist has to have more types of clothing in the reserve than he intends to photograph.
Thus, for a fashion story that has ten pages (therefore, ten outfits), you have to have prepared, ready to use, at least fifteen.
And in addition that the photos the clothes work in combination with other garments, all of them different from those that are used in reality.
All this must be taken into account when designing the outfit.
Honza Pokorný assured us that the image and the style represent alone, in many cases, half of the success.
It is enough to look at Madonna, who is not exactly an extraordinary singer, but the image and marquetin have made her a world star.
In the Czech Republic, at the moment, there is still no clear tendency to use the services of stylists.
Even celebrities also find it useless (my skills are enough for me, my physical appearance is not so important).
And when someone asks us for our services, we have to keep in mind that it is very likely that they will tell us a very different size to theirs (minor).
Then there’s only going to guckle and find out if the heart’s magazines have already written on the subject, if a certain celebrity has fattened/thinned, etc.
On Sunday, Honza and Mario insisted that the stylist does not need to orient himself in fashion, but has to understand an outfit.
During his work, above all he must communicate with the people he saw, so it is essential to be a good psychologist.
He knows how to value people, he doesn’t miss, he defends their opinions.
"When a director hires you to classify the wardrobe and complete it with beautiful clothes, you can't catch and throw away everything there was and say, "there's what a horror."
"Find at least a couple of things that you can ponder and recommend so someone can put them on," Mario says.
He himself also showed us that everything must fit in the so-called "placovka", that is, the job board.
It is fixed around the waist and you have all the necessary tools there.
They are objects such as scissors, scissors, linters, or unmissables. There is also nylon thread (which serves the stylist during the photo shoot of products such as bags or hats), special clamps of latching garments in front, if it is older (pins and other types of hitches are not allowed, because they could damage the fabric), or a sewing set.
In order not to stay in passive listening and put something into practice, we have learned to line the sole of shoes.
Even during photo shoots in the studio, on a flat surface, you could damage the sole and even more the outside.
And we did nothing but coate and clad.
We couldn't touch the shoes with the scissors so we couldn't accidentally damage them.
So you had to be very skillful.
Mario has given me a joy to praise my unreserved work.
The truth is, I'm not very good at those skills.
This is just a small part of everything we’ve listened to throughout the weekend, in the second part of the course.
I have already realized that dedicating myself to styling at a professional level is not a path of pink, but I don’t care exactly what people say.
Need for Speed: The Run competes all over America.
Review
A trip, in principle carefree, is complicated because of a series of careless carelessness of a routine trip during tomorrow’s shift.
To a certain extent expectations were met, but this is useless, if, in reality, it was not intended to do anything extraordinary.
The new installment, to which the title is added The Run, raised great expectations already before its premiere.
He promised that he would give new airs to the old Need for Speed racing saga and, as a result, it appears as a game that shouldn’t end up being just an action genre again.
We are also curious to know how the inserted scenes would look, where the main character descends from the car and walks on his own foot.
As usually happens in the NFS series, the results don’t vary much from what we expected.
There are races that can be considered acceptable, but in total computation points are lost due to absurd failures, which have already appeared in the series for years.
In fact they cannot even be called errors, but rather the incomprehensible reluctance of programmers.
The adventure starts very well.
He introduces you to a story, whose protagonist, Jack, has certain personal problems; to solve them, he is offered to participate in an illegal race throughout America.
You sit at the wheel on the west coast, in San Francisco, and your mission is to get to New York.
The idea is to offer something interesting.
The route is divided into ten stages and then into more than fifty races.
It follows that each race takes place along a different route and the stages are located in different environments, which are quite diverse and interesting.
In this way, one does not even remotely have the feeling that the game always offers the same thing.
Some of the environments are even pleasing to the view, although the technical level of the chart is equivalent to that of previous installments of the series.
So it's nothing of the other world.
But the walk through the desert, the autumn landscape or the high mountains covered with snow produce a very pleasant visual effect.
In addition, races diversify from time to time by an atypical element.
Thus, for example, in the desert you find a sandstorm that decreases visibility.
On the other hand, in the mountains you have to be careful not to bury an avalanche.
According to that, each of the races is very well developed.
There's only a couple of models, but that's enough.
For a moment, you try to overtake a number of demanded rivals (normal in a classic race), then you try to gain time (timed classical duel) and then a duel awaits you against a single opponent.
In the midst of all this sometimes appears the police, who only make things even more difficult.
Novelty is landscapes outside the car.
They present interactive animations when Jack, in most cases, has to escape from someone and you have to help him, always pressing the button right at the right time.
Nothing complicated.
It is surprising, however, that there are far fewer landscapes in the game than you might expect (in particular there are only three).
But the final result is positive, because this element does not become annoying and, in the aforementioned context, it is one of the elements that makes the game more interesting.
The driving model follows in the traces of previous episodes.
That means that today is no longer a big deal, but you can’t claim to be bad.
If you are looking for a realistic simulation, you can already search elsewhere.
But to a race conceived with enough action it is quite good for this driving style, although we can find something better among the games of the competition.
So far, everything in order.
Problems arise after some time.
Contrary to the correctness of driving models, the same thing no longer happens with collisions.
Games of this type cannot be expected to recreate deformations and complicated collisions, but in fact before a blow against any object, you can not predict how your car will react, with which not everything is in order.
It is typical that, when making a very tight overtaking or circulating the car with normal traffic, there are only slight frictions, but in other almost identical situations, your car ends up doing uncontrolled pirouettes.
Or it even ends up totally destroyed.
Thanks to the reset system, there are no big problems, but it can put you in a bad mood.
The resets are programmed in such a way that, when you suffer an accident or leave the track, the game restores you to the last rescue point on the track.
However, in each race only five available resets are available.
If you consume them all, you have to restart the race from the beginning.
So it's nothing more than an aid in case something doesn't go well, but it's not too trusted.
Sometimes, neither reset helps, it only helps to learn the given stage of memory.
A great disadvantage of the game is that the same facts are repeated in different places.
In some curves, for example, you have to enter in a specific way; otherwise, they are impossible to take.
Other times you are somewhere "civile" vehicles always with the same configuration, even if you are the first, fifth or arrive five minutes before or after.
This makes it angry especially in situations, when you see that two cars that meet in opposite directions, your opponent advances without problems, but when you arrive, you have to turn or brake.
It’s the same when you arrive, because it’s programmed because the “surprise” will always happen in front of your noses.
Adversaries also have one more advantage.
During the whole game you will come to places where, without taking into account the moment, the same opponent will always overtake you in the same place.
In addition this happens at the end of the game, on a long bridge, which is even more shocking.
Your opponent must arrive before you, at whatever price.
When it goes in front of you, it makes it difficult for you to see the cars that come head-on, so at the beginning you can porridge your car.
You can understand the idea of creating a game with maximum doses of suspense and adrenaline, but the execution is so apparent that it will surely disappoint you right away.
And it’s a shame, because even if the model of the trip is simple, the game is fun and with action, so it’s often not possible to follow in detail what’s happening or where.
And it doesn't really matter, if the merit takes the idea with fifty exclusive tracks or qualifying in the race so it doesn't fit the boring, or anything else.
An unusual idea is the change of cars during racing.
You have to keep an eye out for gasoline pumps next to the road, because right there you have to change cars, although in the vast majority of cases it will suffice what you have.
Cars are divided into three categories.
Sporters are suitable for urban areas, American strong cars for straight highways and exotic supercars for technical driving, e.g. curved mountain roads.
In addition main narrative thread also appears a thread of parallel challenges, that is, there are races in specific places that you will know for the stories.
Here you will get not only medals, but also experience points for your profile, which serves both challenges and stories.
Upon reaching the upper level, the driver opens up several possibilities, starting with the car and finishing with backgrounds for the profile.
At the same time, an online Autolog function is connected, which compares your results with those of other players and has other community functions available.
One of the hardest things to understand is how the last race in history is done.
With the car you reach the subway tunnel (pass), where you start running in the dark on the tracks (pass).
The speedometer marks between 150 and 200 km/h (pass) and, suddenly, from behind you the convoy of the subway arrives and takes you ahead without more.
In the wording we will surely have a discussion about this for several days, about whether during the programming of the game none thought even a bit or if the real authors take us for a bunch of fools.
The technical part of the game is nothing extraordinary, but at least the overall visual effects result in most pleasant cases, sometimes even superb.
Well, it’s a shame that, in the most tense moments the image quality is reduced and, sometimes, in a serious way.
This mainly affects the accidents where many participants are involved, when the continuous image quality is no longer valid.
The audio is fine and the soundtrack is a matter of taste.
In order to please most of the youth group, the soundtrack belongs to the category "each of his father and mother", but it can be assumed that no one would buy the game just for their music.
The final sensation of Need for Speed: The Run is therefore quite confusing.
If the game avoided absolutely silly mistakes, we’d have trouble claiming that The Run is NFS’ best game in recent years.
It feels that the game isn’t finished.
The fun is assured, but prepare because the errors will hit you in your eyes with the force of airport reflectors.
The choirs of the Carolina University will participate in the "Students of Velvet" concert.
The joint celebration of International Student Day and the anniversary of the Velvet Revolution as a musical experience will take place for the third time at the Festa Academica festival.
During it, twenty choirs will be presented from secondary and university centers.
The festival revolves around two concerts on November 17.
"The Carolina University has a high participation in the festival."
Among the current choirs are the choir of the Faculty of Pedagogy and the Faculty of Humanities, in the committee of the festival is the rector Václav Hampl, "said the head of the organization, Jakub Čaloun.
The summit of the entire festival is free admission for all audiences to the concert of the secondary choirs, which will be held on March 17 at 14 hours in front of the National Technical Library in Dejvice.
The program has the participation of Czech jazz player Karel Růžička and his Celebration Jazz Mass.
In the evening will be held in the venues of the Municipal House in Vynohrady the concert "Velvet Students", in which university choirs will participate, including the choir of the Carolina Uninversity.
The Festa Academica aims not only to dignfully celebrate the International Day of Students and commemorate the 22nd anniversary of the Velvet Revolution, but also to present choral music to the public at the highest level and promote collaborative creation among young people.
The main organizer is the Czech Coral Union in collaboration with the Jan Kepler Secondary Institute.
All the events were supported by the mayor of Prague, Bohuslav Svoboda, and the rector of the Carolina University, Václav Hampl.
The Festival will take place between 16 and 20 November between Prague and Pardubice.
The calendar offers, in addition to the celebratory concerts, a whole series of musical events, improvised student shows and morning concerts.
Those interested can find more information on the festival page www.festaacademica.cz
Ambassador to the EU, Vicenová:
Czechs have a reputation as negativists and Eurosceptics.
"The Lisbon Treaty has significantly affected the balance between individual institutions"
"I didn't expect to set up an all-out war."
"It will last five, six years, before the situation stabilizes a bit, calms down and the new players get used to their new roles," the Czech ambassador to the EU, Milena Vicenová, began with conviction.
How not to take seriously his motto "clearly and openly about Europe", which he said already in the first part of his conference, when he managed to describe every body of the EU and its relations with such precision and clarity, since it would be the envy of many speakers of the Faculty of Law of U. Carolina.
Vicenová also pondered the work of the new permanent president of the European Council, Herman van Rompuy:
"The first comes the criticisms, that if you're bland, a gray official, able to assume any role, but I have to say that it left everyone baffled, because it assumes its roles perfectly."
"He's a man who knows how to listen to members of the twenty-seven states, communicate with them and who has a very clear view of where the EU should go."
The new position of representative of foreign policy and security is explained from the question: "Who is this EU? What number can I call it?" It is therefore an important step towards the unification and clarification of political union for states such as China or India.
No one wants to ban us from Olomouc cheese
Vicenová has also taken care of the agenda, continues and will follow the European Council in the near future.
The Czech presidency two years ago was a success.
The Czechs dealt with the emerging economic crisis, resolved the gas crisis and organized a summit for the Eastern Partnership.
The fall of the government at the time was identified as a very negative aspect, which seriously affected the Chequia.
Czech representation in the EU currently has many compromises.
In the words of the ambassador: "a good fuss", not only the presidency, but also the financial crisis, which is being dealt with now.
On the other hand, we must approve the seven-year budget of the EU, caused by the current economic situation, much more complicated.
If the budget is simpler and more effective, which sectors will have priority, which countries will receive greater support and what less? That is something that will be present on the agenda of the next meeting.
The ambassador also recalled her main slogans, with which she arrived in Europe: "About Europe clearly".
"The truth is that I don't like ugly abbreviations, foreigners or jargons that people don't understand."
"How can a citizen understand that cucumber cucumbers do not really invent curved or round cucumbers, bananas of various sizes or that no one is going to ban Olomouc cheese?"
It also aims to take more advantage of the EU environment and bring more Czech citizens closer to the European institutions.
Europe awaits us from speeds
According to the ambassador, the Czechs have a reputation for Eurosceptics and people perceive rather the negative aspects than the positive ones.
In addition, it regretted the low participation of Czechs in the European institutions.
The fault lies with a multitude of factors, such as the modesty of our candidates, their inability to write messages of motivation, but also the little support of the Czechs.
In addition to the success of the Czech presidency, it highlighted the strength and collaboration of the Visegrad Group.
"Believe me that when they come to me a Pole and a Hungarian and a Slovak approaches me, a Frenchman next to me says: "What, you have already stayed, those of Visegrad's Group?", and it can be seen that it is not funny to him."
In the future, the EU, according to Vicenová, is awaited by very harsh budgetary policy regulations for the Member States.
It is perceived as something very real of the concept of the two speeds, if they are no more, in Europe, more than that of "the European Federation".
“We have countries in the Eurozone and countries outside the Eurozone.”
“We have the Schengen area and we also have the cooperation procedure strengthened.”
"It was said for the first time that only the countries they want and those who don't, that they are left out."
"These procedures will become more and more and will strengthen the two-speed Europe," Vice-Nová is expected.
In this sense, he also highlighted the role of the Czech Republic and Herman van Rompuy in the application of the principle, according to which all issues affecting the whole of the EU should be discussed among member states, not only among Eurozone members.
Brand story:
Innovative IBM begins its second century of existence
If someone was looking for a term that would define IBM's strategy with great precision, the most approximate would be "long-term."
For the general public, IBM is the symbol of a technological revolution, a company that is perceived as current and, however, it has been a hundred years since its foundation.
The basis of this long-placist character was put by the first head of the firm, the visionary Thomas J. Watson Sr.
He already coined the motto that many problems in the world have a solution if people are willing to think.
His motto "Think!" became his label, around which the life of the future giant will be built (it was also the title of an internal magazine that IBM began publishing in 1935).
Watson was also the basis of a carefully raised company culture.
"For us, IBM entails long-term thinking, an ongoing movement in the direction of the future.
IBM has survived and thrived for a hundred years for that reason, because it remained true to its basic principles, but without fearing the changes around.
This has allowed us, during our first century, to transform technology, business and society.
We look forward to thriving even more in our second century," said Samuel J. Palmisano, the current director of the company.
Sophistified system
Watson, already in the 30’s, was concerned about the care of his employees as Baťa’s businessman in Chequia (IBM employees were among the first U.S. operatives who enjoyed paid vacations, insurance, sleek uniforms and a sophisticated remuneration system that rewarded the best inventors and vendors.
Long-term sophistication is maintained by IBM in the customer relationship.
Already from the beginning the company knew how to uncover talent (being one of the first global companies to end any type of discrimination, I could choose without problems).
In line with the anti-discrimination strategy is IBM’s current plan, for which Palmisano will be replaced next year by a woman: Virginia Rometty.
She has been working for thirty years at IBM, where she has been head of sales, marketing and strategies.
In recent years IBM has participated in so-called virtual encounters, online brainstorming, from which countless future strategies and innovations arise.
It is not surprising that they come up with ideas, because almost half a million people work in the firm.
An institution with a good reputation
The fixed position in the business provides the company with a strong internal and external image.
"From the beginning, IBM maintained a concept of an institution rather than a technology company," says Harvard Business School economist professor and author of the IBM book Rosabeth Moss Kanter.
“IBM is not a technology company, but a company trying to solve business problems for technology users,” says George Colony of Forrester Research.
As the company itself says there is a difference between getting into the business and directly creating a business.
IBM - or the "Big Green" - as it is known in the U.S. familiarly because of its logo, has become in the last hundred years one of the largest companies in the world.
It is arguably the most versatile technology company (develops both equipment and programs, infrastructures and web hosting services within a wide range of services, ranging from servers to nanotechnology).
It holds the highest number of patents from all U.S. tech companies and five of its employees have received the Nobel Prize.
Among his inventions are ATM, payment cards, financial swaps, barcodes and floppy disks.
IBM will bill 220 billion dollars this year. This year it has become the second technology firm by market capitalization (the first is Apple), when it first surpassed Microsoft in 1996.
Looking to the Future
Not all products and innovations have just satisfied the taste of customers and the moment (IBM did not bet on its own operating system, OS/2, Prodigy online services or IBM PCjr computers).
“If your business is based on moving forward, it can’t be emotionally anchored in the past,” said Samuel J. Palmisano.
That’s why IBM has no problems building its bases on other platforms (and equally, if they don’t work, it abandons them).
And this the difference of the competition, Microsoft, which basically stays and falls always exclusively with Windows.
Technology of the future
In terms of sales, IBM is mainly dedicated to services, of which approximately one-fifth are from programs and another fifth of equipment.
However, even in 1990 equipment accounted for more than half of the supplier share.
Since 2000, IBM has sold low-yielding assets for a total value of US$15 billion. During the same period, it has invested US$58 billion in the purchase of future technology.
Investments have continued since 2008, when the modern global financial crisis first manifested.
IBM acts according to the premises of its first boss, Thomas J. Watson, who during the great economic crisis of 29 increased investments.
It seems that so far IBM has managed to weather the crisis.
IMB’s share value since the beginning of 2008 has grown stratospherically to 120%, the company’s net profit has continued to rise.
IBM’s currency is to change everything except its value.
You can therefore hope that when the next crisis comes, this flexible giant will endure.
IMB’s Story: From Cheese Mower to Spaceflight
IBM (International Business Machines) was founded in New York a hundred years ago, its original name Computing Tabling Recording Corporation.
The name IBM was adopted as early as 1924 – it was originally a brand used in branches in Canada and South America.
The base that gave rise to the birth of IBM arises from the merger of four companies dating back to the 1880’s.
He possessed inventions such as the famous "signing clock", which allows to control the entry and exit of employees.
The architect of the new company was businessman Charles Ranlett Flint, who until 1930 also presided on his supervisory board.
Flint signed the head of a competing company, Thomas J. Watson, to assist him with the company’s management.
The new leader overshadowed IBM’s founder (Watson’s ideas remain the firm foundation on which corporate culture and identity are based).
Watson ran the company until 1952.
IBM, as its name suggests, began with the production and sale of all kinds of business appliances, from meat and cheese cutters to cash registers.
During the first four years that Watson led the company, turnovery doubled by 9 million dollars and the great expansion of the company over the continents began.
Watson was so crucial to the company that, almost after forty years occupying the boss’ chair, he was replaced by his son, Thomas Watson Junior.
Under his direction, IBM began working on the development of artificial intelligence and developed the first programming language.
In the 1960s IBM personnel and computers helped NASA guide flights into space (to Mercury, Saturn and in 1969 the famous flight to the Moon).
Meanwhile, in 1964 IBM developed the first generation of computers, the IBM System/360 series.
The classic "fish", which established the computer standard of that time, came to the market under the name IBM 5150 in 1981.
Twenty years later, IBM sold its production of computers to the Chinese company Lenovo, which, for its part, acquired the consulting part of the company Pricewaterhouse Coopers and began to offer a complete advice and services of high added value.
IBM’s strategy over the past three years is the Smarter Planet concept, that is, “a smarter planet.”
Its objective is to make more rational use of technology, although areas have not yet been planned and there has been no circumstances, for example with regard to city transport and administration.
For the commerce sector, IBM recently unveiled the “Smart Commerce” platform that allows retailers to manage the entire business cycle.
IBM has a long history in this country.
Already in 1932 he opened a branch in Czechoslovakia at that time, the first country that had it in Central and Eastern Europe.
Today, the IBM ČR also operates the strategic outsourcing centre in Brno.
The headquarters for Central and Eastern Europe is in Prague. Also here is a world-renowned research team working with voice recognition.
Rychtářová about her unfaithful husband:
Iveta, keep that donkey, I don't want it anymore!
Darina Rychtářová (53) said it's over!
After her husband Josef Rychtář (53) had become Iveta Bartošová's only protector (45), but also her lover, Darina was still hopeful that Josef would wake up from his pink sleep and return home.
However you will no longer wait and have established clear rules for life in the future.
“Pepe can come back home, but no longer as my partner,” Rychtářová explained.
When Darina Rychtářová welcomed Bartošové into her home during the summer, she couldn't even imagine how her marriage would end.
Despite the request, Iveta had not moved thirty days after Říčany and Pepe did not abandon the singer.
He even publicly stated that he loved her.
Eventually, Darina resigned herself, seemingly accepted her husband’s relationship and even said goodbye to him forever.
Rychytář doesn't care who his wife sleeps with.
If Rychtář one day broke up with Bartošová, his wife would not wait for him at home with open arms.
He is the biological father of my children and, if he wants to live the rest of his life in our house, no one will throw him out."
"But here I would live no longer as my dear and old puddler who was mistaken, but as a man to whom I am united with certain ties," Rychtářová said, adding that she had already disengaged from her husband and insisted only on mutual respect.
Josef doesn't care if she's a woman locked the back door.
"I accept my wife's decision."
“I’ll be with Iveta and there’s no change possible.”
"My wife established this as a marriage on paper and I respect it."
"The company is still in effect, I make the house arrangements, I take care of the garden, the home, I do the shopping."
"Darina and I spoke normally, the only thing is that we don't share a bed," Rychtář said.
If Rychtářová were to find a new love, he wouldn't object.
"We don't sleep together and she doesn't interest me, or where she's going or if she has any boyfriends.
"I know it's my fault, I fell in love with Iveta and I take full responsibility," Josef concludes.
Women’s Worst Vices: Do They Also Mean You?
If you ask men to be able to cite some typical vices of women, in general each of them will name them without thinking.
Dear women, do you recognize yourselves in the following lines, where certain female vices that manage to boil the blood of men are cited?
Go shopping
Do you reproach your half-orange that you have dependence on purchases?
Do you have to buy at least one rag per week?
Do you often like to buy on sale?
Then in your case it can be said that shopping has become a vice.
Some women realize they should appease their passion for shopping, at least a bit.
But to see, which woman could resist the temptation to walk simply through clothing stores, look for well-tightened garments and then try them all in the taster (ideally in all different colors)?
Although for most women going shopping is a hobby, for men it can practically become hell.
Just remember how many times you’ve already told your partner that you’ll best wait in front of the door.
Constant dissatisfaction
"Aren't I too fat?"
“I’d need to lose weight for at least five kilos – should I start exercising?”
"Do you really like me?"
Don't these phrases sound to you?
What do you do?
So she's one of those women obsessed with her looks.
It’s not that you should stop taking care of yourself, but many men are allergic to listening to their partner complain all the time about their physical appearance.
Strong sex also agrees that the more the frequency of complaints increases, the more annoying women become.
Order and cleaning in the first place
It's like an infinite merciful.
Wipe windows, vacuum, scrub the floor, remove dust, scrub the bathtub and all that at least twice a week.
Do you reproach your partner for stepping on the clean floor with a dirty feet, your children who have soiled a freshly wiped washbasin and a shelf with glass doors that cost you so much to clean?
In case you suffer from this "deviation", try to be aware that nothing should be exaggerated and that order and cleanliness surely should not be paramount in the family.
This harmless desire for cleansing could threaten your relationships and family well-being.
Make nasty comments
"Used underpants are left with dirty clothes."
"You also want to wear those used socks tomorrow"
"The wet rag is not left on the ground!"
If you make those comments to your partner more times a day, know that you will get them out of their boxes.
Naturally, you don’t want to say anything bad, you just want to get everything in order.
Maybe, if men knew about this, women, for their part, wouldn’t make so many comments.
Slanders and gossips
Some women also have slanders, gossips, but also offenses and conspiracy against someone.
Women focus on relationships, that's why they like to talk together about things like who, where, with whom, how and why.
Maybe each of us sometimes escapes a harmless little gossip.
With his hand in his heart, this is typical of almost all women.
On the other hand, there are gossip women of those who are not controlled, who love gossiping and do so often despise everyone and are dangerous to those around them, especially in a women’s work team.
